{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Migrate kafka and rabbit sink modules from Spring XD to the spring-cloud-stream (s-c-s) module repository, restructured as Spring Boot apps using the s-c-s programming model (@EnableBinding with the Sink interface) and published under new Maven coordinates (org.springframework.cloud.stream.module).",
    "Implement per-channel binder support (U3) on top of the spring-cloud-stream binder abstraction, allowing rabbit, redis, or kafka binders to be configured independently for input/output channels via module properties.",
    "Implement external configuration overrides (U4) via a Spring Boot properties/YAML file loaded by the module launcher, supporting overrides such as alternate Maven coordinates for module resolution.",
    "Refactor the Cloud Foundry SPI deployer (U5) to use the reactor-based CF java-client (v2) instead of the legacy v1 client, keeping the existing deployer SPI contract intact.",
    "Implement Hadoop distribution selection (U6) through Maven profiles / classifier-based dependency sets (e.g., default, hdp, cdh, phd) so the correct Hadoop client libraries are placed on the classpath at build/packaging time.",
    "Move header-enricher (U7) into the XD proper codebase as an internal module, preserving its existing option names and behavior.",
    "Upgrade the dependency BOM (U8) to Spring Framework 4.2.1, Spring Integration 4.2, and Spring AMQP 1.5, resolving deprecations and API breakages introduced by the upgrades."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "A single experienced developer (familiar with Spring XD, spring-cloud-stream, Spring Integration, and CF) performs all work; estimates are effort, not calendar time.",
    "Existing XD source code, module repositories, and build infrastructure are available and accessible; no greenfield development is required.",
    "Per-activity estimates include design, implementation, unit tests, and activity-level integration tests; dedicated cross-module system testing is estimated as a separate activity.",
    "Test environments are available: embedded/local kafka and rabbit, a redis instance, a Cloud Foundry foundation for deployer testing, and at least two Hadoop distributions for classpath validation.",
    "No user interface changes are required; all features are driven via configuration and deployer SPIs.",
    "Target platform for these modules is Java 8 / Spring Boot 1.x era consistent with XD and SI 4.2 (the Java 17 note in the specification refers to Spring Framework 6.0 and does not apply to this increment).",
    "Code review, project management, and release coordination overhead are excluded; documentation effort for end users is included as a separate activity."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Requirements analysis and architecture design",
      "activity_description": "Analyze all eight user stories, define the target module structure in the s-c-s repo, the binder configuration model, the external override mechanism, and the CF deployer refactoring approach; produce design notes to guide implementation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "U1: Migrate kafka sink module from XD to s-c-s repo",
      "activity_description": "Port the kafka module code to the spring-cloud-stream Sink model, adapt configuration properties, create the new Maven module and build config, add unit tests and an integration test against embedded kafka, and verify it works as a sink in a streaming pipeline.",
      "most_likely_effort": 40
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "U2: Migrate rabbit sink module from XD to s-c-s repo",
      "activity_description": "Port the rabbit module code to the spring-cloud-stream Sink model, adapt configuration properties, create the Maven module, add unit tests and an integration test against a local rabbit broker, and verify sink behavior in a streaming pipeline. Reuses patterns established in A2.",
      "most_likely_effort": 32
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "U3: Support different binder types per module channel",
      "activity_description": "Design and implement per-channel binder configuration so rabbit, redis, or kafka binders can be plugged independently as source or sink; implement property binding, binder wiring, unit tests, and integration tests covering mixed-binder channel combinations.",
      "most_likely_effort": 56
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "U4: External configuration file overrides for modules",
      "activity_description": "Implement loading of an external properties/YAML config file that overrides default module configurations, including module resolution from alternate Maven coordinates; add precedence handling, validation, unit tests, and integration tests with a sample override file.",
      "most_likely_effort": 40
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "U5: Refactor CF SPI deployer to CF java-client",
      "activity_description": "Replace the legacy CF client usage in the Cloud Controller SPI deployer with the reactor-based CF java-client v2, redesigning request/response and error handling while preserving the deployer SPI contract; add unit tests with a mocked client and integration tests against a real CF foundation; measure basic performance improvement.",
      "most_likely_effort": 80
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "U6: Selectable Hadoop distribution support",
      "activity_description": "Introduce build profiles / dependency classifiers for supported Hadoop distributions, ensure the correct Hadoop client libraries are placed on the classpath, document the selection mechanism, and validate startup and basic HDFS access against at least two distributions.",
      "most_likely_effort": 48
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "U7: Move header-enricher module into XD proper",
      "activity_description": "Relocate the header-enricher processor from the modules repository into XD proper, adjust build wiring and module registration, preserve existing options and behavior, and migrate/extend its unit and integration tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "U8: Upgrade to SI 4.2, Spring 4.2.1, and AMQP 1.5",
      "activity_description": "Update the dependency BOM and build files to Spring Integration 4.2, Spring Framework 4.2.1, and Spring AMQP 1.5; resolve compilation issues, deprecations, and behavioral changes; run affected module test suites and fix regressions.",
      "most_likely_effort": 40
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "Cross-module integration and system testing",
      "activity_description": "Perform end-to-end verification of the increment: build streaming pipelines using the migrated kafka/rabbit sinks with mixed binders, exercise external config overrides, deploy via the refactored CF deployer, and validate Hadoop distribution selection on the upgraded dependency stack.",
      "most_likely_effort": 40
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "Build and CI configuration updates",
      "activity_description": "Update CI plans, module publishing, and packaging for the new s-c-s modules, Hadoop profiles, and upgraded dependencies; ensure reproducible builds and artifact publication.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A12",
      "activity_name": "Documentation and release notes",
      "activity_description": "Write reference documentation for the migrated sinks, binder configuration, external overrides, Hadoop distribution selection, and upgrade notes covering SI 4.2 / Spring 4.2.1 / AMQP 1.5 changes.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 448
  }
}
```

